    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d995">

                <pb facs="1154" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg958"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/7–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 995<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chief of the Division of
                        Economic Security Controls</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Oliver</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chief of the Division of Economic Security Controls</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Rubin</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d995-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27">July 27 [1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. For Rubin from Oliver.</p>
                <p>AmLegation Bern believes that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> on Swiss reported Deptel
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi>
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] 122 July 25<anchor n="2" xml:id="d995-f2"
                    /> would tend to discourage Swiss cooperation in tracing and disclosing German
                    assets. Bern adds that unlike Spain there is little prospect of dissipation in
                    Switzerland. A similar reaction it is predicted will be received from Stockholm.
                    Would <pb facs="1155" n="959" xml:id="pg959"/> appreciate your reactions based
                    on Bern visit. ES considers Swiss already aware
                    of our general position. Recently Swiss Chargé urged deletion<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d995-f3"/> of Scintilla, majority stock in which is German [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]. Oliver
                    told him control under Swiss freezing decree not sufficient for deletion and
                    intimated occupying powers would have to consider their rights to German shares.
                    Chargé intimated Switzerland would help if deletion could be expected. At this
                    stage consider telegrams from various sources apt to confuse missions. Suggest
                    your reply be sent only to Department.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d995-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d995-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Secretary of State at Babelsberg over the signature of Grew.</p>
            </note>
